HISTORY_VERSION 1.0.0

TYPE Foundation

STATUS APPROVED

DATE 2026-07-06

TITLE

PACE's own Mission and Vision written down as versioned artifacts.

WHY

PACE had evolved a mature, clear sense of its own purpose across this
session's conversation — what problem it solves, who it's for, what it
governs, what's expected of it — but none of that lived anywhere durable.
It existed only in chat, which is precisely the failure mode PACE itself
exists to prevent: knowledge trapped in a conversation, gone the moment
the conversation is gone.

DECISION

Wrote governance/PACE_MISSION_0.1.0.pdl and governance/PACE_VISION_0.1.0.pdl,
both STATUS APPROVED. Mission: PACE does for a project's knowledge what
Git did for its source code — solving engineering knowledge scattered
across chats, Slack, Notion, documents and people's memory, lost every
time the team, the AI, or enough time changes. Vision: any AI should be
able to reconstruct any of PACE's governed projects in minutes, not by
"remembering" but because the project can explain itself; states six
concrete expectations (fast AI onboarding, knowledge that never gets
lost, every AI reconstructing identical context, projects surviving
decades of team turnover, pace create producing a fully-formed project
in minutes, and PACE learning continuously).

Updated governance/README.md to clarify that the abstract
GOVERNANCE_PROTOCOL stays name-free (universal rules), while PACE's own
Mission/Vision are a different kind of artifact — assertions about
PACE's own identity — and so, like any Mission/Vision assertion in the
Ontology, do carry an OWNER.

Noted explicitly in the Vision document: expectation 6 ("PACE learns
continuously") is not a new capability requirement — it already has a
home in ontology/PACE_ONTOLOGY_0.1.0.pdl's PROMOTED_FROM relation
(Decision | Policy | Protocol | Standard <- Request), discovered while
writing this Vision rather than designed for it. The ontology anticipated
this before the Vision named it explicitly.

IMPACT

PACE's own purpose is now a durable, versioned artifact instead of
something that only survives if this conversation is remembered.

NEXT_STEPS

Per the roadmap: a minimal CLI wrapping the Kernel (pace doctor, pace
context), then pace init, then adopting TuPeríMetro as the first
governed project.

APPROVED_BY

President Cley Duarte

END
